<template><section class="page-heading"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Field guide / 02</p><h1>About the project</h1><p>A small, transparent encyclopedia for people who want to look closer.</p></div></section><section class="container text-page"><h2>Curiosity with a paper trail.</h2><p>The Penguin Project is an independent educational website about penguin species, their habitats, and the adaptations that make them extraordinary. It is designed to be inviting first and rigorous underneath.</p><div class="policy-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Editorial promise</p><h3>Original, understandable writing</h3><p>Profiles are written for curious visitors rather than copied from reference works. Important claims point back to a dated source.</p></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Image promise</p><h3>Credits stay close</h3><p>Images are registered locally with creator, source, license, review status, and accessible alt text. This first release uses original project illustrations.</p></div></div><p class="note">Content last reviewed: 23 November 2026 · Taxonomy and conservation assessments may change over time.</p></section></template>
